{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461682-v5-rebuilding-the-sabbat-campaign","id":1461682,"title":"[V5] Rebuilding the Sabbat campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-27T07:42:35-07:00","id":1461682,"title":"[V5] Rebuilding the Sabbat campaign","content":"I've already started a new MIAMI BY NIGHT campaign this week with already a few sessions underway. The premise is that a pair of Lasombra women have been trapped in the Underworld for the past two decades and they emerge in Miami, Florida only to find that the Second Inquisition have purged the city and the Sabbat that have survived are a bunch of suicidal nutjobs. Furthermore, that the time in the Abyss has caused them to lose hold of their Paths somehow. It will become a question of what a Sabbat means and how they will adapt to this new world.<br /> <br /> This book is very helpful to that.<br /> <br /> I think their goal I will &quot;nudge&quot; them to will be to join the Church of Caine and Anarchs to form a New Sabbat out of the ashes of the old. I'm curious about what people think might be good themes to explore in this game and what sort of conflicts might arise.<br /> <br /> Groups I know I want to deal with:<br /> <br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Church of Caine<br /> * Ravnos<br /> * Lasombra defectors<br /> * Talley<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T16:18:49-07:00","id":1461771,"title":"","content":"Silly answer<br /> <br /> -Kill them<br /> -Convert them<br /> -Kill them<br /> -Kill them<br /> -Kill him, Very very slowly and very publicly as a warning to every other lasombra traitor.<br /> <br /> Serious answers<br /> How old are the PC's? are they on a path? Personally I'd infiltrate the Anarchs are they're probably the easiest to pass as. I'd also start making more lasombra as soon as the chance arrises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T16:51:48-07:00","id":1461775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461682-v5-rebuilding-the-sabbat-campaign#post1461682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already started a new MIAMI BY NIGHT campaign this week with already a few sessions underway. The premise is that a pair of Lasombra women have been trapped in the Underworld for the past two decades and they emerge in Miami, Florida only to find that the Second Inquisition have purged the city and the Sabbat that have survived are a bunch of suicidal nutjobs. Furthermore, that the time in the Abyss has caused them to lose hold of their Paths somehow. It will become a question of what a Sabbat means and how they will adapt to this new world.<br /> <br /> This book is very helpful to that.<br /> <br /> I think their goal I will &quot;nudge&quot; them to will be to join the Church of Caine and Anarchs to form a New Sabbat out of the ashes of the old. I'm curious about what people think might be good themes to explore in this game and what sort of conflicts might arise.<br /> <br /> Groups I know I want to deal with:<br /> <br /> * Anarchs<br /> * Church of Caine<br /> * Ravnos<br /> * Lasombra defectors<br /> * Talley</div> </div> </div> </div>Intuitively, I would say that these two Lasombra women have deep feelings (of some kind) for each other and that they stayed sane in the Abyss by social companionship that could have also been a love affair. If one or both followed Power And The Inner Voice and they were in competition for position in Vampire society before leaving Earth, things get really interesting. Maybe their ability to function without a Path is an effect of having been trapped in the Abyss together and that this will wear off over time. If one of them begins to practice P&amp;IV, they must consider exploiting the other's love/friendship to remain true to Path... despite also caring for the other. <br /> <br /> You could make a list of Subjects of Conversation that the two Lasombra talked about during their ordeal. Determine what kind of Character Voice each has, their worldview and perspective on things. Pick one of those subjects and then write some dialogue that has already passed between them. Have it that the words they spoke have some kind of power (the way Order of Hermes Mages think of words having power, for comparison). The conversations they had influence the world in some supernatural way that affects the players. Perhaps the crazy Sabbat and the Inquisitors are playing out some debate they had. PCs must uncover what was said between them and both Vampires shared secrets that would put them in jeopardy if the wrong Cainites (or Wraiths even) found out.<br /> <br /> Themes: Love, Loyalty, Power, &quot;All the World's a Stage&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T17:17:13-07:00","id":1461777,"title":"","content":"That will be up to the players as they are the PCs.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But both players have expressed their desire to roleplay dealing with the Sabbat and how it has changed from Revised to V5's version. I've already got a few ideas:<br /> <br /> * Seeking out Lucita<br /> * Finding out about the Lasombra defection<br /> * Describing the Sabbat having &quot;degenerated&quot; from the savage but erudite group it was.<br /> * The Gehenna War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T18:35:57-07:00","id":1461784,"title":"","content":"It is hard to say what could the themes be because it depends a lot on those PCs. Since they will come back with everything they had before stripped from them, it will be a very introspective chronicle at first, then evolve out of their decision on what to make of it.<br /> <br /> The first thing you could do would be preparing a few NPCs that they'll recognize as Sabbat members, but covering at least four previous reactions to the schism: defectors to the Camarilla, defectors to the Anarchs, ex-Sabbat Autarkis and fully lost Sabbat. Better if those characters avoid contact, so they don't have to deal with the conflict of dealing with former brothers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T01:18:27-07:00","id":1461930,"title":"","content":"Really depends on how skilled/social you Lasombra are. Of course they've been nerfed to Oblivion so... <br /> <br /> My Strat. <br /> <br /> Step 1- Embrace/Ghoul a quick force. Blood bond and indoctrinate. Put your tentacles into mortal spheres. <br /> Step 2- Approach the remnants/Anarchs to find their stances. Butcher the obvious problems and take the willing. Leave the fence sitters for now. <br /> Step 3- make an example of the SI and traitors. <br /> Step 4- Convince/pressure/Press Gang/make examples of the fence sitters. <br /> Step 5- The folks who stood out, let them have the privilege of the Vauldrie. Grant these &quot;true&quot; sabbat the thralls you've picked up along the way. <br /> Step 6- Use your massive organizational advantage (the Vauldrie and Dominate) to lock down the city. From there you can develop and send out crusades. to nearby cities. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T16:35:33-07:00","id":1462041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461682-v5-rebuilding-the-sabbat-campaign?p=1461777#post1461777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat will be up to the players as they are the PCs.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How developed is the story of having been in the Abyss? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461682-v5-rebuilding-the-sabbat-campaign?p=1461777#post1461777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But both players have expressed their desire to roleplay dealing with the Sabbat and how it has changed from Revised to V5's version. I've already got a few ideas:<br /> <br /> * Seeking out Lucita<br /> * Finding out about the Lasombra defection<br /> * Describing the Sabbat having &quot;degenerated&quot; from the savage but erudite group it was.<br /> * The Gehenna War.</div> </div> </div> </div>It used to be that you were not considered &quot;True Sabbat&quot; until you had killed at least one Vampire of an enemy Sect. I ran a game with new characters where most of the targets in nearby cities had been eliminated. The Bishop had to come up with other objectives that would allow the PCs to pass the membership test. The more successful the Sabbat are at taking over territory, the more they become responsible for governing that territory. They cannot help but consider adopting practices that the Camarilla used to control mortal society. The Camarilla has the Masquerade. The Sabbat have Sect Security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}